        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.086,
            0.883,
            0.126
          ],
          "content": "**3. What is the total amount Krithika has, if she has the following numbers of notes of ₹100, ₹20 and ₹5? Complete the following table:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.141,
            0.205,
            0.157
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.159,
            0.872,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": "| No. of100Notes | No. of 20notes | No. of ₹5notes | Expression and total amount(in ₹) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 3 | 5 | 6 | $\\begin{array}{c}3 \\times 100 + 5 \\times 20 + 6 \\times 5 \\\\= 430\\end{array}$ |\n| 6 | 4 | 3 | $\\begin{aligned}6 \\times 100 + 4 \\times 20 + 3 \\times 5 \\\\= 695\\end{aligned}$ |\n| 8 | 4 | Z | $\\begin{array} { c } { 8 \\times 1 0 0 + 4 \\times 2 0 + z \\times 5 } \\\\ { = 8 8 0 + 5 z } \\end{array}$ |\n| X | y | Z | $\\begin{array}{c}x \\times 100 + y \\times 20 + z \\times 5 \\\\= 100x + 20y + 5z\\end{array}$ |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_26_table_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.473,
            0.883,
            0.583
          ],
          "content": "**4. Venkatalakshmi owns a flour mill. It takes 10 seconds for the roller mill to start running. Once it is running, each kg of grain takes 8 seconds to grind into powder. Which of the expressions below describes the time taken to complete grind ‘y’ kg of grain, assuming the machine is off initially?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.599,
            0.308,
            0.619
          ],
          "content": "(a) $10+8+y$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.359,
            0.599,
            0.669,
            0.619
          ],
          "content": "(b) $(10 + 8) \\times y$ (c) $\\mathbf { 1 0 \\times 8 \\times y }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.633,
            0.309,
            0.652
          ],
          "content": "(d) $1 0 + 8 \\times y$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.36,
            0.633,
            0.489,
            0.652
          ],
          "content": "$1 0 \\times y + 8$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.67,
            0.331,
            0.689
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** (d) 10 + 8 × y"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.706,
            0.883,
            0.77
          ],
          "content": "**5. Write algebraic expressions using letters of your choice. (a) 5 more than a number (b) 4 less than a number (c) 2 less than 13 times a number (d) 13 less than 2 times a number**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.788,
            0.205,
            0.805
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.8,
            0.594,
            0.914
          ],
          "content": "Let letter ‘d’ represent the number, then (a) $d + 5$ (b) $d - 4$ (c) $1 3 \\times d - 2$ (d) $2 \\times d - 1 3$"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.492,
